oh my god you can't even do what you  want  there was a time early on in the  twilight franchise that kristen stewart  and robert pattinson were forbidden to  be lovers  from being forced to miss significant  life events to being fired over a small  breach of contract the cast of twilight  had to follow all sorts of strict rules  in order to stay with the franchise  which broken rule resulted in a  different actress playing victoria in  the third film  it's my birthday right now  the team behind twilight really  considered having pattinson take on the  role of edward cullen after he did an  audition with kristen stewart where the  chemistry could not be ignored the  electricity between the actors was in  fact a bit too good it was so spicy that  director catherine hardwick had to  remind the actors that the movie reading  was pg-13 sure there were no sticky  situations pattinson was told he had to  keep his distance from his co-star  especially because she was underage at  the time that they met we all know they  didn't stay apart for too long though  there was immediate chemistry between  the two of you  yeah yeah  one rule kristen stewart wasn't a fan of  at all was having to wear uncomfortable  and visually limiting colored contacts  it was really difficult for the actress  to focus while performing since she was  having a tough time seeing but  ultimately she didn't have a choice in  the matter stewart wasn't the only one  though  loads of twilight actors had to endure  the same requirement and none of them  enjoyed it  doing the twilight films was a full-time  commitment which resulted in actors  having to miss some pretty significant  life events to be on set instead kristen  stewart was forced to skip her own high  school graduation ceremony  the filming of bella's grad scene  happened to coincide with stewart's  actual graduation  so instead of ignoring her own milestone  completely the actress had a mini  ceremony on set an extra was set to  shake stewart's